WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.580
Speaker 1: The Republican primary field is
very quickly getting much more crowded, including

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:07.690
with two very interesting new entrants.

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:12.650
Mike Pence expected to announce he will run
against his own former president under whom

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:13.650
he served.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:18.320
And Chris Christie is going to announce that
he is entering this race, which is very, very

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:22.220
interesting for other reasons, which I will
talk about in a moment.

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:24.330
We will start with Mike Pence.

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:25.640
Mike Pence reports.

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:33.840
NPR expected to announce 2024 run for president
on June 7th at an event in Des Moines.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:37.190
According to a source familiar with the campaign.

00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:42.710
I am sure that it will be an electric atmosphere
when Mike Pence makes this announcement.

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:44.440
No, it won't.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:47.590
It will be quite the opposite, but it will
be an interesting announcement nonetheless.

00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:49.699
And we'll talk about why in a moment.

00:00:49.699 --> 00:00:50.710
NPR rates.

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:54.570
Pence has been signaling his plans for several
months, with several stops in early voting

00:00:54.570 --> 00:01:00.320
states like New Hampshire and Iowa and the
announcement of a superPAC supporting his

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:01.320
bid.

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:05.890
Pence will join at least nine other Republicans
attempting to unseat Trump as the frontrunner

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:07.530
for the Republican nomination.

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:10.800
Now, what will Pence's campaign look like?

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:16.409
Because if you serve as vice president to
Trump and then you run against him, you can't

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:20.690
do the thing that Nikki Haley and Tim Scott
and others are doing where you don't criticize

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:21.690
Trump, Right?

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:27.240
If you're saying I disagree so much with the
guy I served under that I will run against

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:28.240
him.

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:29.960
You have to explain what your disagreements
are, I think.

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:30.960
NPR writes.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:35.759
In the past several weeks, Pence's previewed
a campaign focused on returning the Republican

00:01:35.759 --> 00:01:41.979
Party to traditional Republican themes like
expanding free markets, fiscal responsibility,

00:01:41.979 --> 00:01:44.860
supporting American allies abroad and small
government.

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:49.439
He has made more pointed attacks on Trump,
his former running mate, by invoking his own

00:01:49.439 --> 00:01:56.350
faith and family values and promising to respect
to respect the Constitution.

00:01:56.350 --> 00:02:02.990
Here is an MSNBC NBC News report of the moment
when news of this broke.

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:08.539
Speaker 2: We have breaking news regarding
a new entry into the already crowded republican

00:02:08.539 --> 00:02:09.590
race for president.

00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:13.800
We told you last hour that on tuesday chris
christie was getting in.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:18.050
Now on Wednesday, former vice president mike
pence.

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:20.489
NBC's john allen has the very latest.

00:02:20.489 --> 00:02:22.910
He's breaking this story and joins me on the
phone.

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:24.820
John, what can you tell us?

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:35.190
I can tell you Mike Pence is in as of a week
from today.

00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:42.920
He will be doing a video probably in the morning
and then a march speech in Des Moines, Iowa.

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:47.709
He was very focused on Iowa, as are a lot
of campaigns, as a place that they believe

00:02:47.709 --> 00:02:51.480
is very hospitable to the former vice president
or because of its strong evangelical Republican

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:52.480
base.

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:54.920
So he'll be doing that speech sometime on
on the seventh.

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:56.950
And then there is going to be a town hall
later that night.

00:02:56.950 --> 00:02:57.950
Okay.

00:02:57.950 --> 00:02:59.400
Speaker 1: So that is the CNN town hall.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:04.849
Last week, we we thought that Pence was going
in this direction because we knew CNN had

00:03:04.849 --> 00:03:07.430
scheduled a Republican town hall with Pence.

00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:11.599
And we said to ourselves, would they be doing
that if this guy was not going in the direction

00:03:11.599 --> 00:03:12.599
of running?

00:03:12.599 --> 00:03:16.940
So currently currently, Mike Pence is running
in fourth place.

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:18.380
We have the latest polling here.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:23.379
As you can see, the big purple line at the
top is Trump at 53%.

00:03:23.379 --> 00:03:27.620
The green line sort of in the middle of the
screen is DeSantis at 22.

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:30.900
So Trump 53, DeSantis 22.

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:34.930
Then it's Nikki Haley at about four and a
half percent.

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:43.269
And after Nikki Haley is Mike Pence at 3.8%
just ahead of Vivek Ramaswamy.

00:03:43.269 --> 00:03:47.120
Will the announcement get some new support
for Mike Pence?

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:48.770
It might a couple of points worth.

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:50.640
I would I would expect.

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:55.439
But is this going to be a big shakeup to the
Republican primary?

00:03:55.439 --> 00:03:56.569
I don't think so.

00:03:56.569 --> 00:04:01.959
And part of it has to do with the fact that
many of the very people.

00:04:01.959 --> 00:04:04.569
Who are not on the MAGA side.

00:04:04.569 --> 00:04:09.269
Don't see Pence as the strongest alternative.

00:04:09.269 --> 00:04:13.470
Partially because Pence, even though he may
be displeased with some of the way that Donald

00:04:13.470 --> 00:04:16.540
Trump managed the presidency or whatever.

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:17.540
Pence is too close.

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:23.520
If you want to go anti MAGA, you probably
don't go with the MAGA vice president.

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:28.120
As much distance as Pence would like to put
between himself and Trump.

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:36.120
So the question is going to be for the MAGA
group, is there an alternative to Trump?

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:40.979
I doubt it would be Pence because many of
those MAGA people are mad that Pence quote

00:04:40.979 --> 00:04:48.630
didn't send it back to the States in in 2020
to try to prevent Joe Biden from becoming

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:52.539
president in 2020 and 2021, even though he
really couldn't do that.

00:04:52.539 --> 00:04:56.240
And so it's unlikely that they would say,
well, we really are MAGA, we want something

00:04:56.240 --> 00:05:00.169
better, so we'll go with pence because they
see pence as an enemy, quite frankly, thanks

00:05:00.169 --> 00:05:02.210
to the rhetoric from Donald Trump.

00:05:02.210 --> 00:05:07.000
On the other hand, the anti MAGA people would
likely go with someone who was never affiliated

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:08.000
with Donald Trump.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:11.259
So I don't exactly see how Mike Pence is going
to get anything out of this.

00:05:11.259 --> 00:05:19.169
Mike Pence, as I believe in his early in his
early 6060s, Mike Pence, age a 63.

00:05:19.169 --> 00:05:25.509
So I don't know if Pence is calculating that
if he wants to do this, he'd rather do it

00:05:25.509 --> 00:05:31.711
at age 63 rather than 67 and maybe closer
to when he is more of a household name, maybe

00:05:31.711 --> 00:05:34.490
fifth thinking by 2028.

00:05:34.490 --> 00:05:36.180
Maybe people will have forgotten about me.

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:37.180
I don't know.

00:05:37.180 --> 00:05:39.770
Again, I don't exactly know what Pence is
thinking.

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:42.590
I see the campaign as dead on arrival.

00:05:42.590 --> 00:05:47.530
But let's now talk about a much more interesting
campaign than that of Mike Pence.

00:05:47.530 --> 00:06:59.490
Let's talk 

00:06:59.490 --> 00:07:06.620
about Chris Christie.

